Koios recovery source. Exact source and design-evidence identities, exclusions,
and semantic adaptations are recorded in TRANSFER.toml.

The iterative multi-objective optimization block originates in the PhD work of Eugene
J. Ragasa and is reconstructed from evidence scattered across PyPosPack and multiple
research repositories.

This product includes adapted Pareto-selection, Gaussian KDE, Gaussian-mixture
partitioning, cluster-conditioned sampling, and covariance-repair behavior from
PyPosPack, Copyright (c) 2017 Eugene Ragasa, distributed under the BSD 2-Clause License.
The source header credits Dmitriy Morozov of Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory
with Pareto performance improvements contributed in December 2016. The retained
license text is in licenses/PyPosPack-BSD-2-Clause.txt.
